      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "To convert the spherical coordinates $(\\rho, \\theta, \\phi) = \\left( 3, \\frac{5 \\pi}{12}, 0 \\right)$ to rectangular coordinates, we use the following formulas:\n\\begin{align*}\nx &= \\rho \\sin \\phi \\cos \\theta \\\\\ny &= \\rho \\sin \\phi \\sin \\theta \\\\\nz &= \\rho \\cos \\phi\n\\end{align*}\nPlugging in the given values, we have:\n\\begin{align*}\nx &= 3 \\sin 0 \\cos \\frac{5 \\pi}{12} = 3 \\cdot 0 \\cdot \\cos \\frac{5 \\pi}{12} = 0 \\\\\ny &= 3 \\sin 0 \\sin \\frac{5 \\pi}{12} = 3 \\cdot 0 \\cdot \\sin \\frac{5 \\pi}{12} = 0 \\\\\nz &= 3 \\cos 0 = 3 \\cdot 1 = 3\n\\end{align*}\nTherefore, the rectangular coordinates corresponding to the spherical coordinates $(\\rho, \\theta, \\phi) = \\left( 3, \\frac{5 \\pi}{12}, 0 \\right)$ are $(\\boxed{(0, 0, 3)})$.",
