      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "Given the point $(\\rho,\\theta,\\phi) = \\left( 3, \\frac{5 \\pi}{12}, 0 \\right)$ in spherical coordinates, we can convert it to rectangular coordinates by using the following equations:\n\n$$x = \\rho \\sin \\phi \\cos \\theta$$\n$$y = \\rho \\sin \\phi \\sin \\theta$$\n$$z = \\rho \\cos \\phi$$\n\nFrom the given spherical coordinates, we have $\\rho = 3$, $\\theta = \\frac{5 \\pi}{12}$, and $\\phi = 0$.\n\nPlugging these values into the equations, we have:\n\n$$x = \\rho \\sin \\phi \\cos \\theta = 3 \\sin(0) \\cos\\left(\\frac{5\\pi}{12}\\right) = 0$$\n$$y = \\rho \\sin \\phi \\sin \\theta = 3 \\sin(0) \\sin\\left(\\frac{5\\pi}{12}\\right) = 0$$\n$$z = \\rho \\cos \\phi = 3 \\cos(0) = 3$$\n\nTherefore, the rectangular coordinates of the point are $(0, 0, 3)$, which we can box as $\\boxed{(0, 0, 3)}$.",
